    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: 30 July 2026</em></p>

    <p>LAMBATY respects your privacy and is committed to handling personal data responsibly. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, why we use it, when it may be shared, how long it is retained, and the choices and rights available to you.</p>

    <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
    <p>This website and online store are operated by LAMBATY Establishment, a business registered in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia under Commercial Registration number 7049721033.</p>
    <p>For the purposes of this Privacy Policy, "LAMBATY," "we," "us," and "our" refer to LAMBATY Establishment.</p>
    <p>Privacy questions and requests can be sent to: <a href="mailto:info@lambaty.sa">info@lambaty.sa</a></p>

    <h2>2. Scope of This Policy</h2>
    <p>This Privacy Policy applies when you visit lambaty.sa, place or attempt to place an order, contact us, request support, submit a return or refund request, or otherwise interact with LAMBATY through our website and related services.</p>
    <p>Third-party websites, applications, and services may have their own privacy policies. We encourage you to review those policies when using services provided by third parties.</p>

    <h2>3. Personal Data We Collect</h2>
    <p>Depending on how you interact with LAMBATY, we may collect the following categories of personal data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Identity and contact information</strong>, such as your name, email address, mobile number, and billing or delivery address.</li>
      <li><strong>Order and transaction information</strong>, such as products ordered, order number, payment status, transaction reference, delivery status, and refund information.</li>
      <li><strong>Account information</strong>, if customer accounts are enabled, such as login details and saved preferences.</li>
      <li><strong>Customer support information</strong>, including messages, questions, troubleshooting details, and any photos or videos you choose to provide.</li>
      <li><strong>Return and refund information</strong>, including the reason for a request and evidence needed to review product condition or damage.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical and usage information</strong>, such as IP address, browser type, device information, pages viewed, referral source, timestamps, and website interaction data.</li>
      <li><strong>Cookie and preference information</strong>, including language, session, checkout, analytics, and marketing preferences where enabled.</li>
      <li><strong>Marketing preferences</strong>, including whether you have chosen to receive promotional communications.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How We Collect Personal Data</h2>
    <p>We may collect personal data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Directly from you</strong> when you place an order, complete a form, contact us, or request support.</li>
      <li><strong>Automatically</strong> through cookies, server logs, and similar technologies when you use the website.</li>
      <li><strong>From service providers</strong> involved in operating the store, processing payments, preventing fraud, delivering orders, or providing customer support.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Why We Use Personal Data</h2>
    <p>We use personal data only for clear and appropriate purposes, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Processing, confirming, fulfilling, and delivering orders.</li>
      <li>Processing payments, refunds, and transaction records.</li>
      <li>Communicating about orders, delivery updates, support requests, returns, and refunds.</li>
      <li>Providing product setup, app connection, and technical support.</li>
      <li>Operating, maintaining, improving, and securing the website and checkout process.</li>
      <li>Detecting or preventing fraud, misuse, security incidents, or unauthorized transactions.</li>
      <li>Complying with accounting, tax, legal, regulatory, and record-keeping requirements.</li>
      <li>Understanding website performance and customer experience through appropriate analytics.</li>
      <li>Sending marketing communications where you have consented or where otherwise permitted by applicable law.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The legal basis used will depend on the activity and may include performing a contract with you, complying with a legal obligation, protecting legitimate interests where permitted, or obtaining your consent where required.</p>

    <h2>6. Payments</h2>
    <p>Payments are processed through Tap Payments and the applicable banks, card networks, wallets, or other payment providers available at checkout. Shopify may also support the technical operation of the checkout and order system.</p>
    <p>LAMBATY does not intentionally collect or store your complete payment-card number or security code. Full payment details are handled by the relevant payment provider. We may receive limited information such as payment status, transaction reference, payment method, and partial card information where made available for order management, fraud prevention, or support.</p>
    <p>Payment providers process personal data under their own terms and privacy policies.</p>

    <h2>7. Shipping and Delivery</h2>
    <p>To fulfil and deliver your order, we may share necessary information with Aramex or another approved delivery partner. This may include your name, mobile number, delivery address, city, order reference, shipment details, and delivery instructions.</p>
    <p>Delivery partners use this information to create shipments, contact you where necessary, provide tracking, complete delivery, and address delivery-related issues.</p>

    <h2>8. When We Share Personal Data</h2>
    <p>We may disclose personal data only where necessary and appropriate, including to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Shopify and related technology providers that host or operate parts of our online store.</li>
      <li>Tap Payments, banks, card networks, wallets, and payment-service providers.</li>
      <li>Aramex or another approved shipping and fulfilment provider.</li>
      <li>Email, hosting, security, analytics, customer-support, and information-technology providers.</li>
      <li>Accountants, auditors, legal advisers, insurers, or other professional advisers where necessary.</li>
      <li>Government, regulatory, judicial, or law-enforcement authorities where disclosure is legally required or permitted.</li>
      <li>A successor or purchaser in connection with a lawful business transfer, subject to applicable requirements.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>LAMBATY does not sell personal data to advertisers or unrelated third parties.</p>

    <h2>9. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
    <p>Our website may use cookies and similar technologies to keep the store functioning, remember preferences, protect checkout, understand website performance, and support advertising or marketing where enabled.</p>
    <p>Essential cookies may be required for functions such as navigation, security, cart management, checkout, and language preferences. Where required, non-essential analytics or marketing cookies will be used only after an appropriate choice or consent is obtained.</p>
    <p>You can manage cookies through the website preference tool, where available, or through your browser settings. Disabling certain cookies may affect website functionality.</p>

    <h2>10. Marketing Communications</h2>
    <p>We may send promotional emails or messages only where you have requested them or where otherwise permitted by applicable law. You can unsubscribe at any time by using the unsubscribe option in the message or contacting us at <a href="mailto:info@lambaty.sa">info@lambaty.sa</a>.</p>
    <p>We may still send non-promotional communications that are necessary for your order, payment, delivery, account, support request, or legal obligations.</p>

    <h2>11. International Processing and Transfers</h2>
    <p>Some technology, payment, hosting, analytics, or support providers may process or store personal data outside Saudi Arabia. Where this occurs, LAMBATY will take reasonable steps to use providers and safeguards that support compliance with applicable Saudi data-protection requirements.</p>

    <h2>12. Data Retention and Destruction</h2>
    <p>We retain personal data only for as long as it is needed for the purpose for which it was collected, to complete transactions and support requests, to protect legal rights, or to meet tax, accounting, regulatory, and record-keeping requirements.</p>
    <p>When personal data is no longer required, we will take reasonable steps to delete, destroy, or anonymize it in accordance with applicable requirements. Backup copies may remain for a limited period until they are securely overwritten or deleted through normal system processes.</p>

    <h2>13. Data Security</h2>
    <p>We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards designed to protect personal data from unauthorized access, loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure. These safeguards may include access controls, secure service providers, encrypted connections, account protection, and internal access limitations.</p>
    <p>No website, transmission method, or storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure. You are responsible for keeping any account credentials confidential and for notifying us if you suspect unauthorized activity.</p>

    <h2>14. Your Personal Data Rights</h2>
    <p>Subject to the Saudi Personal Data Protection Law and other applicable requirements, you may have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Be informed about the legal basis and purpose for collecting and processing your personal data.</li>
      <li>Request access to personal data held about you.</li>
      <li>Request a clear and readable copy of your personal data where applicable.</li>
      <li>Request correction, completion, or updating of inaccurate or incomplete personal data.</li>
      <li>Request destruction of personal data when it is no longer needed, subject to lawful retention obligations.</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent for processing that relies on consent, without affecting processing already completed before withdrawal.</li>
      <li>Object to or restrict certain processing where such rights apply under applicable law.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To submit a privacy request, contact <a href="mailto:info@lambaty.sa">info@lambaty.sa</a></p>
    <p>We may need to verify your identity before completing a request. We will respond within the period required by applicable law. Certain rights may be limited where retaining or processing the information is required by law or necessary to protect legal rights.</p>

    <h2>15. Children and Legal Capacity</h2>
    <p>The LAMBATY store is intended for customers who have the legal capacity to enter into a purchase. We do not knowingly seek to collect personal data directly from children. A parent or legal guardian should complete any purchase or contact on behalf of a minor where required.</p>

    <h2>16. Third-Party Links and Services</h2>
    <p>The website may link to third-party services, including payment providers, delivery tracking, app stores, or the LotusLamp X application. LAMBATY is not responsible for the privacy practices of independent third parties. Please review their privacy policies before providing personal data to them.</p>

    <h2>17. Complaints</h2>
    <p>If you have a concern about how we handle personal data, please contact us first at <a href="mailto:info@lambaty.sa">info@lambaty.sa</a></p>
    <p>You may also have the right to submit a complaint to the Saudi Data & AI Authority or another competent authority in accordance with applicable law.</p>

    <h2>18. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy when our services, providers, practices, or legal obligations change. The updated version will be published on this page with a revised "Last updated" date. Material changes may also be communicated through the website or another appropriate channel.</p>

    <h2>19. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      LAMBATY Establishment<br>
      Commercial Registration: 7049721033<br>
      Dhahran, Saudi Arabia<br>
      Email: <a href="mailto:info@lambaty.sa">info@lambaty.sa</a>
    </p>
    <p>We aim to acknowledge general inquiries within 1-2 business days. Privacy-rights requests will be handled within the period required by applicable law.</p>
